Assert-LastExitCode 'Cosmos DB verification'

az search service show -g $workloadRg -n $search `
    --query '{name:name,state:status,public:publicNetworkAccess,localAuthDisabled:disableLocalAuth,sku:sku.name}' -o table
Assert-LastExitCode 'Azure AI Search verification'

az network private-endpoint list -g $workloadRg `
    --query '[].{name:name,state:privateLinkServiceConnections[0].privateLinkServiceConnectionState.status,subnet:subnet.id}' -o table
Assert-LastExitCode 'Private endpoint verification'

#!markdown
## 22 — Verify project identity roles and AAD connections

#!pwsh
az role assignment list --assignee $projectMi --all `
    --query '[].{role:roleDefinitionName,scope:scope}' -o table
Assert-LastExitCode 'Project ARM role verification'

az cosmosdb sql role assignment list -g $workloadRg -a $cosmos `
    --query "[?principalId=='$projectMi'].{principalId:principalId,roleDefinitionId:roleDefinitionId,scope:scope}" -o table
Assert-LastExitCode 'Cosmos SQL role verification'

az rest --method GET `
    --url "https://management.azure.com${stdId}/projects/${stdProject}/connections?api-version=2025-06-01" `
    --query 'value[].{name:name,category:properties.category,auth:properties.authType,target:properties.target}' -o table
Assert-LastExitCode 'Project connection verification'

#!markdown
## 23 — Mandatory DNS checkpoint

Run this cell only from a Zava-connected host, VPN, ExpressRoute path, or peered VNet using the approved resolver. Confirm `ipconfig /all` shows the expected Zava DNS servers.

**Stop** if any service resolves publicly, times out, or returns an address outside the private endpoint subnet.

#!pwsh
ipconfig /all
ipconfig /flushdns

$namesToResolve = @(
    "$stdFoundry.cognitiveservices.azure.com",
    "$stdFoundry.openai.azure.com",
    "$stdStorage.blob.core.windows.net",
    "$cosmos.documents.azure.com",
    "$search.search.windows.net"
)
foreach ($name in $namesToResolve) {
    Write-Host "`n--- $name ---" -ForegroundColor Cyan
    Resolve-DnsName $name -ErrorAction Stop | Format-Table Name, Type, IPAddress, NameHost -AutoSize
}

#!markdown
# One-time capability hosts

Do not continue until private endpoints, DNS, roles, and AAD connections have passed verification.

#!markdown
## 24 — Confirm capability hosts do not already exist

Both lists must be empty before initial deployment. If either contains a host, do not deploy the two-host template.

#!pwsh
az rest --method GET `
    --url "https://management.azure.com${stdId}/capabilityHosts?api-version=2025-06-01" `
    --query 'value[].{name:name,state:properties.provisioningState}' -o table
Assert-LastExitCode 'Account capability-host lookup'

az rest --method GET `
    --url "https://management.azure.com${stdId}/projects/${stdProject}/capabilityHosts?api-version=2025-06-01" `
    --query 'value[].{name:name,state:properties.provisioningState}' -o table
Assert-LastExitCode 'Project capability-host lookup'

#!markdown
## 25 — Display, validate, and preview capability hosts

Expected what-if: exactly one account capability host and one project capability host.

#!pwsh
Get-Content $hostTemplate
az bicep build --file $hostTemplate --stdout | Out-Null
Assert-LastExitCode 'Capability-host Bicep compilation'

$hostParameters = @(
    "workloadName=$workload",
    "environment=$environment",
    "networkResourceGroupName=$networkRg",
    "vnetName=$vnet",
    "agentSubnetName=$agentSubnet"
)
